# 1️⃣ Job Sequencing Problem

## 📖 Problem

You are given:

```text
Job ID
Deadline
Profit
```

Each job takes:

```text
1 unit time
```

Goal:

```text
Maximize total profit
```

while completing jobs before deadlines.

---

### Example

```text
Job   Deadline   Profit

A        2        100
B        1         19
C        2         27
D        1         25
E        3         15
```

---

# 2️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Sort jobs by:

```text
Profit (Descending)
```

Then schedule every job at the latest available slot before its deadline.

Why?

```text
Higher profit jobs
should get priority.
```

---

# 3️⃣ Example

Sorted by profit:

```text
A 100
C 27
D 25
B 19
E 15
```

Schedule:

```text
Slot 1 → C
Slot 2 → A
Slot 3 → E
```

Total Profit:

```text
142
```

---

# 4️⃣ C++ Code

```cpp
struct Job
{
    int id;
    int deadline;
    int profit;
};

bool compare(Job a, Job b)
{
    return a.profit > b.profit;
}

int jobScheduling(vector<Job>& jobs)
{
    sort(
        jobs.begin(),
        jobs.end(),
        compare
    );

    int maxDeadline = 0;

    for(auto job : jobs)
    {
        maxDeadline =
            max(maxDeadline,
                job.deadline);
    }

    vector<int> slot(
        maxDeadline + 1,
        -1
    );

    int totalProfit = 0;

    for(auto job : jobs)
    {
        for(int j = job.deadline;
            j > 0;
            j--)
        {
            if(slot[j] == -1)
            {
                slot[j] = job.id;
                totalProfit += job.profit;
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    return totalProfit;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N²)

Space: O(N)
```

