# 5️⃣ Minimum Platforms

## 📖 Problem

Given arrival and departure times of trains.

Find the minimum number of platforms required so that no train waits.

---

### Example

```text
Arrival:

900 940 950 1100 1500 1800

Departure:

910 1200 1120 1130 1900 2000
```

Output:

```text
3
```

---

# 6️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Sort:

```text
Arrival Times
Departure Times
```

Use two pointers.

If:

```text
arrival <= departure
```

Need one more platform.

Else:

```text
departure finished
```

Platform becomes free.

---

# 7️⃣ C++ Code

```cpp
int findPlatform(
    vector<int>& arr,
    vector<int>& dep)
{
    sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());
    sort(dep.begin(), dep.end());

    int i = 0;
    int j = 0;

    int platforms = 0;
    int answer = 0;

    while(i < arr.size() &&
          j < dep.size())
    {
        if(arr[i] <= dep[j])
        {
            platforms++;
            answer =
                max(answer,
                    platforms);
            i++;
        }
        else
        {
            platforms--;
            j++;
        }
    }

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Sorting: O(N log N)

Traversal: O(N)

Total: O(N log N)
```

