# 8️⃣ Jump Game

## 📖 Problem

Given an array:

```text
nums[i]
```

represents maximum jump length from index i.

Determine whether you can reach the last index.

---

### Example

```text
nums = [2,3,1,1,4]
```

Output:

```text
True
```

Because:

```text
0 → 1 → 4
```

---

# 9️⃣ Greedy Observation

Maintain:

```text
farthest reachable index
```

If current index becomes greater than:

```text
farthest
```

Then:

```text
Cannot proceed
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool canJump(
    vector<int>& nums)
{
    int farthest = 0;

    for(int i = 0;
        i < nums.size();
        i++)
    {
        if(i > farthest)
        {
            return false;
        }

        farthest =
            max(
                farthest,
                i + nums[i]
            );
    }

    return true;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(1)
```

