# 🔟 Jump Game II

## 📖 Problem

Find minimum jumps needed to reach the last index.

Example:

```text
nums = [2,3,1,1,4]
```

Output:

```text
2
```

Path:

```text
0 → 1 → 4
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Maintain:

```text
Current Range
```

and:

```text
Farthest Reach
```

When current range ends:

```text
Take one jump
```

and update range.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int jump(vector<int>& nums)
{
    int jumps = 0;

    int currentEnd = 0;
    int farthest = 0;

    for(int i = 0;
        i < nums.size() - 1;
        i++)
    {
        farthest =
            max(
                farthest,
                i + nums[i]
            );

        if(i == currentEnd)
        {
            jumps++;
            currentEnd =
                farthest;
        }
    }

    return jumps;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N)

Space: O(1)
```

